course: dictionary
lesson: 14204
title: Mucky and friends
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words are informal. People use them in chatty talk with family and friends, not in exams or formal letters. Mucky is one of these words, and it is common in British, Irish and Australian family talk. «Wash your mucky hands before tea!» Mum is not being rude. The word tells you the hands are dirty, and the words around it, wash and before tea, give you the clue.
explain: Mucky can also mean slightly naughty. «Dad laughed at the mucky joke, but Gran said it was not for children.» A mucky joke is rude in a cheeky way. Here the clues are laughed and not for children, which show the joke was a bit rude but not very serious.
explain: Mucky can describe the weather too. «It was a mucky day, so we stayed in.» Stayed in is the clue: nobody wants to go out on a day that is wet, grey and unpleasant. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Dirty would not make sense for a day, so the meaning must be wet and grey.
fact: Mucky is an adjective, so it describes a noun: mucky boots, a mucky pup.
fact: «Mucky» means dirty, muddy or messy.
fact: «Mucky» can also mean slightly rude and naughty, like a mucky joke.
fact: «Mucky» can describe weather that is wet, grey and unpleasant.
fact: Mucky is informal, so use it in chatty talk, not in formal writing.
exercise: «Wash your mucky hands before you eat!» What does mucky mean here? | Hungry and tired | *Dirty and muddy | Clean and shiny | Cold and wet
exercise: Dad says, «That was a mucky joke!» What does mucky suggest? | *Slightly rude and naughty | Very funny and kind | Long and boring | Sad and quiet
exercise: «It was a mucky day, so we stayed in.» What kind of day was it? | Windy and bright | Hot and sunny | Dark and starry | *Wet, grey and unpleasant
test: In «mucky boots», which word is the noun that mucky describes? | *boots | mucky | take off | at the door
test: Ella's gran says «mucky pup» to a child who has been playing in the mud. What does mucky pup mean? | *A messy child | A cheeky dog that barks | A clean and tidy child | A sleepy puppy
exam: Which meaning fits «a mucky day» in a story about a walk in the rain? | Bright and warm | *Wet, grey and unpleasant | Very loud | Huge and famous
